Author: cioinside <cioinside@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:26:53 2026 +0300

    feat(opencode-local): fallback model on provider token/quota limit
    
    When a run fails with a provider-side token/quota exhaustion error
    (e.g. MiniMax coding-plan 429), retry once on the configured
    adapterConfig.fallbackModel (provider/model) in a fresh session and
    attribute the result to the model actually used. The detector only
    reads error channels (stderr + type=error events), so task content
    mentioning limits cannot trigger a false fallback. Invalid
    fallbackModel formats are ignored with a logged warning.
    
    Also: opencode v2 has no --variant flag, so the variant now rides on
    the model ref as provider/model#variant (pre-existing uncommitted fix
    in the same hunk).
    
    UI: AgentConfigForm gains an optional 'Fallback model' dropdown for
    opencode_local agents (ModelDropdown label/hint props), plus help text.

